From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: msm8916-samsung-gt510: wake on Home key and cover open

With system suspend enabled only the PMIC power key woke the tablet. Mark
the Home key and the hall sensor (SW_LID) as wakeup sources: pressing Home
or opening a cover resumes from s2idle. The downstream DT marks home_key
with gpio-key,wakeup; the hall sensor is handled there by Samsung's own
flip-cover driver.

Tested: Home wakes from s2idle (gpio-keys event count, clean resume). The
cover path uses the same gpio-keys wakeup mechanism and is untested (no
magnetic cover at hand).
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8916-samsung-gt510.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8916-samsung-gt510.dts
@@ -439,4 +439,16 @@
 
 &usb_hs_phy {
 	extcon = <&muic>;
+};
+
+/*
+ * Wake from suspend with the Home key and when a cover is opened (hall
+ * sensor), as on Android; the power key (PMIC) already wakes.
+ */
+&{/gpio-keys/home-button} {
+	wakeup-source;
 };
+
+&{/gpio-hall-sensor/hall-sensor-switch} {
+	wakeup-source;
+};
